    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full suite is green. Here's a summary of what I changed.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a structured address form (`addressLine1` + optional `addressLine2`, alongside the existing `city`/`postcode`) to `POST /api/owners`, preferred over the flat `address` when present, while keeping the flat form fully backward-compatible.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` to the `OwnerFields` schema (so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` carry them) and removed `address` from the `required` list, since an owner may now supply an address in either form. Updated the `address` description to note it's now the composed/normalized value on the response.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 Added persisted `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` fields with getters/setters (columns `address_line1`, `address_line2`).\n\n3. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added the two new columns to the `owners` table.\n\n4. **`ValidateOwnerFields.normalizeAddress`** \u2014 Rewrote the address handling: it normalizes whichever fields are supplied. When a non-blank `addressLine1` is present it uses the structured form, storing the normalized lines and composing `address` = normalized `addressLine1`, with a single space + normalized `addressLine2` appended when present. Otherwise it falls back to the normalized flat `address`. A request with neither still yields a `400` (`address` error). MapStruct auto-maps the new fields request\u2192entity\u2192response.\n\n5. **`ValidateOwnerFields.validatePostcode`** \u2014 Made the city\u2192region lookup null-safe. The new `structuredOwner()` test payload carries a postcode, so the missing-city case now reaches this code with a null city; `Map.of(...).get(null)` throws NPE (would be a `500`). Guarding it preserves the `400` for the required-field violation.\n\nThe household hash, postcode validation, and locality all read `city`/`postcode` (shared top-level fields populated in both forms) plus the now-composed, normalized `address`, so they use the structured data when present and fall back to the flat address otherwise.\n\n**Tests:** Full suite `55/55` green, including the address checkpoints (Cp01, Cp12, Cp29, Cp30, Cp36, Cp44).\n\nOne note: the PUT `/api/owners/{ownerId}` flow (`ValidateOwner`/`ApplyOwner`) was left on the flat-address path \u2014 it's out of scope for this change and has no tests, but if you want structured-address support on update too, that's a follow-up.",
